    "terminal_reason": "completed",
    "result_text": "I implemented `draft_reply` in `app/drafts.py`. All 5 tests pass, including 3 new ones I added in `tests/test_drafts.py`.\n\n**The request** is set up the same way as `suggest_tag`:\n- model `DRAFT_MODEL`\n- `instructions=STYLE_GUIDE`\n- the ticket's subject and body as the input\n- `max_output_tokens=MAX_DRAFT_TOKENS`\n- `store=False`, so OpenAI doesn't store the response\n- `metadata={\"ticket_id\": ticket.id}`\n\n**The result** is a `Draft` with the ticket id and the reply text with surrounding whitespace removed.\n\n**Truncation:** `truncated` is True only when the response's status is `\"incomplete\"` and the reason given is `\"max_output_tokens\"`. I checked the installed `openai` package, and a response can also be incomplete for other reasons, such as a content filter. Those don't count as truncation.\n\nThe new tests cover the request parameters, the whitespace stripping, a cut-off at the token cap, and a content-filter stop that is not marked as truncated."
